# Figma / GUI parity

**Rule:** Do not add GUI elements, copy, or chrome that are **not** in the Figma mockups or written interface specs derived from them.

## Before adding UI

1. Pick the **layer** you are implementing:
   - Screen composition → `.cursor/gui/views/` (`View / …`)
   - Column slots → `.cursor/gui/panels/` (`Panel / …`)
   - Geometry / variants → `.cursor/gui/components/` (`Atom /`, `Item /`)
2. Fetch the linked **variant-set** node (not the whole canvas `4191:5772`).
3. Do not take colors or extra chrome from a `View /` screenshot when an `Atom /` or `Item /` exists.
4. If a `View /` hides the right column, do not keep File Info in the layout.

If it is not in the mockup or spec, **do not ship it** in the frontend (no “helpful” counters, hints, badges, or debug-style labels).

## Examples

| Do not add (unless spec/Figma) | OK when in mockup/spec |
|-------------------------------|------------------------|
| `showing 2 of 3` pagination hint in grid header | `Files (References)` section title |
| Extra status lines under section headers | Toolbar controls from `4026:4988` |
| Ad-hoc tooltips explaining internal pagination | Empty states named in specs |
| File Info column on Empty DFM Project | File Info Null on Root Folder |

## Specs vs implementation

- **Specs** follow Figma; implementation follows specs.
- `View /` specs say which panels sit together. Panel specs say slots. Atom specs say pixels.
- Backend-driven behavior (pagination, virtualization) may exist **without** extra user-visible labels unless the design shows them.
- If a label is needed for a11y only, use `aria-*` / `sr-only`, not visible copy.

## When Figma is unclear

Ask or update the interface spec first — do not invent visible UI and document it later. Open questions live in [views/architecture.md](../gui/views/architecture.md).
